{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109656-dictum-as-sovereign-4-and-hardened-heart-as-winter-2","id":1109656,"title":"Dictum as Sovereign 4 (and Hardened Heart as Winter 2)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-30T01:14:41-07:00","id":1109656,"title":"Dictum as Sovereign 4 (and Hardened Heart as Winter 2)?","content":"I am wondering just why.<br /> <br /> In other games, the supernatural ability to give orders and be obeyed (with limitations: no self-harming to harm to loved ones) is not considered so powerful that it justifies a level 4 in Discipline or Gifts or, here, Arts.<br /> <br /> Besides, I liked the precision on previous editions about what a &quot;simple command&quot; is: two words. Yes, it means that you have to phrase your order with only two words. When it is more elaborate, then it is a Geas.<br /> <br /> Also, when you consider that Winter 2 allows to resist the effects of Dictum, Sovereign now seems quite the cheap Art.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to another consideration: the new designing of Sovereign is problematic on several levels. I don't like the wording of &quot;Guest List&quot; which doesn't strike me as regal enough for the noble Art par excellence. &quot;Ward&quot; was very good (and also, I think, better presented as the old magic of faerie concealment and protections).<br /> <br /> So: I'm going to keep Sovereign 1: Protocol; 2: Dictum; 3 Grandeur with the idea that Grandeur gives the target a grace and poise and beauty which is for everyone to see. I like the rules version given here, and to me they reflect well my quick-and-dirty rule when Grandeur was used in my games: +1 Appearance per success on the cantrip); 4: Ward, and 5: Geas.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T01:56:01-07:00","id":1109665,"title":"","content":"Graciously SAVED.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T02:58:30-07:00","id":1109674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109656-dictum-as-sovereign-4-and-hardened-heart-as-winter-2#post1109656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am wondering just why.<br /> <br /> In other games, the supernatural ability to give orders and be obeyed (with limitations: no self-harming to harm to loved ones) is not considered so powerful that it justifies a level 4 in Discipline or Gifts or, here, Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but on the other hand instilling feelings of adoration and respect sufficient to prevent others from acting against you is in other games considered powerful enough to be placed at level 5 for an example see Majesty. <br /> <br /> Fae are just better known for enchanting people into adoration than for commanding them directly. Do not forget that Sovereign is a noble art and as such in a way Sidhe art. The Sidhe as nobility are all about being so glorious that they are obeyed not because they overtake your mind, like some lowly vampire, but because they are too magnificent to disobey. That is to say it is more in theme for the Fae, and their concept of nobility, to instill adoration through Grandeur than to force direct commands as per Dictum.<br /> <br /> So basically Sovereign currently goes from instilling manners to acnowledging the grandeur of your host to limiting access to giving direct commands and finally come to instilling geas. Where as the old Sovereign went from instilling manners to commanding to instilling adoration to limiting access to geas. It may be just me, and apparently the writers, to whom the new order seem more in theme for Fae.<br /> <br /> As for the Winter Art. Yes Hardened Heart is powerful but it does also have considerable draw backs in making one cold and unfeeling, which may lead to really bad decisions, and unable to spend willpower. So the choice becomes either giving in to instilled emotions/commands and thus not being yourself or casting all emotions out and thus not being yourself. Fair trade in my eyes. <br /> <br /> Also only the Fae have access to the Winter art which leaves Sovereign to rule over majority of those living in the world of Darkness from prodigals to mortals to the manifold Chimerae of the Dreaming and even those Fae uneducated in the Winter Arts.<br /> <br /> Naturally as we can see here YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T04:08:40-07:00","id":1109683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109656-dictum-as-sovereign-4-and-hardened-heart-as-winter-2?p=1109674#post1109674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but on the other hand instilling feelings of adoration and respect sufficient to prevent others from acting against you is in other games considered powerful enough to be placed at level 5 for an example see Majesty.<br /> <br /> Fae are just better known for enchanting people into adoration than for commanding them directly. Do not forget that Sovereign is a noble art and as such in a way Sidhe art. The Sidhe as nobility are all about being so glorious that they are obeyed not because they overtake your mind, like some lowly vampire, but because they are too magnificent to disobey. That is to say it is more in theme for the Fae, and their concept of nobility, to instill adoration through Grandeur than to force direct commands as per Dictum.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point. I will have to chew on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T04:09:35-07:00","id":1109684,"title":"","content":"So maybe in this order: Protocol, Grandeur, Dictum, Ward and Geas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T09:36:31-07:00","id":1111305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1109656-dictum-as-sovereign-4-and-hardened-heart-as-winter-2?p=1109684#post1109684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So maybe in this order: Protocol, Grandeur, Dictum, Ward and Geas?</div> </div> </div> </div>That works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},